A Markdown file without frontmatter prints its first heading.
== args
input/**/*
== file input/docs/guide.md
---
summary: Guide overview.
---

# Guide
== file input/src/with-comment.md
---
description: Utility helpers for HTTP requests.
---
# fetcher
== file input/src/no-summary.md
# value
== file input/misc/raw.txt
plain text
== stdout
glob view: input/**/*
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/docs/guide.md: summary: "Guide overview."
input/src/no-summary.md: # value
input/src/with-comment.md: description: "Utility helpers for HTTP requests."
== stderr
== exit 0
